; `b` is a lowerable child of lowerable `a`; `c` is a lowerable child of
; lowerable `b`. Two diagnostics, document order: `b` then `c`. (`a` is a forest
; root, never a nested child, so it is not flagged.)
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code lowering_nested_lowerable :path [b lowering])
  (diagnostic :code lowering_nested_lowerable :path [c lowering]))
